 @AndrewTSq  Right, the market is screwy.  I don't know where you live; prices will vary.  According to Steve, though, the 3080 12 GB and the 6900xt are comparably priced, on average, in the US and Australia--or at least they were at the time of filming. 

Typically, you'd compare based on the MSRP market segment of each product--e.g. 3080 vs 6800xt, 6900xt vs 3080ti or 3090--and you'd use stock performance for the basic comparison, with the understanding that third party cards will often offer factory overclocks at a price premium.

But MSRP is meaningless at the moment, which makes comparison difficult.  There's an unavoidable fudge factor.  NVIDIA didn't even name an MSRP for the 3080 12 gb, lol.  It's an orgy of price gouging.

