 @FOEILELIJK  Well, for one. I don't know where you're seeing anyone still using GTA V as a data point, but whatever, sure.

And two, people play it for GTA Online, which has the same pitfalls you describe for Destiny being online only. If an outlet is going to use GTA V as a data point in 2022, it better be for GTA Online or else it's a wasted effort.

Outlets will prioritize newer games with either an in game benchmark if it's representative of the actual game, or an easily reproduced test run. Of course that's not all you see, (R6 Siege is in this video), but that's just how it is. Destiny 2, of course has neither of the above conditions currently. It will today, but that's not the point. Again, I'd like to see Destiny 2 on the list for major outlets to still use, but I can just as easily look for a Destiny 2 specific benchmark video.

